course: dictionary
lesson: 7829
title: Quota: a fixed share or limit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quota is a fixed amount or number of something. It can be a limit, such as how many fish a boat may catch, or a target, such as how many jobs a worker must finish.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. In «If each class has a quota of 5 tickets, 6 classes get 30 tickets», the words each class and 6 classes show that a quota is a share for every group. Try the swap: each class gets its share still makes sense, so quota means a fixed share.
explain: Phrases help too. «Meet the quota» means reach the target, and «over quota» means more than the limit allowed. Quotas often appear in news about fishing, trade and work, so these phrases are worth remembering.
fact: A quota is a fixed amount or number of something.
fact: A fishing quota is a limit on how many fish can be caught, which helps protect fish so they do not run out.
fact: A work quota is a target, such as a salesperson's monthly quota of sales.
fact: «Meet the quota» means reach the target; «over quota» means more than the limit.
fact: In history, «impossible grain quotas (amounts each village had to hand over)» were amounts that were far too much for villages to manage.
exercise: If each class has a quota of 5 tickets, how many tickets do 6 classes get? | 5 | 11 | 56 | *30
exercise: Why do fishing quotas exist? | To stop people from swimming | To make fish taste better | *To help fish not run out | To let fish grow bigger
exercise: «A salesperson has a monthly quota.» What is the quota? | A holiday they must take | A fish they must catch | *A target number of sales to reach in a month | A list of their favourite customers
test: Which phrase means you have reached your target? | Paint the quota | Lose the quota | *Meet the quota | Forget the quota
test: What does «over quota» mean? | *More than the limit allowed | Finished early on a Friday | A quota painted blue | Less than you need to sleep
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to quota when it means a fixed share? | Puzzle | Mistake | Forest | *Share
